Queries 
.heart of interacting with DBs
.act as instructions for:
    .retrieving specific data 
    .filtering results 
    .performing calculations 


Clauses 
.building blocks of powerful queries 
.act as instructions within a statement, specifying actions like:
    .filtering data 
    .sorting results 
    .grouping information 


Operators 
.building blocks for manipulating data within queries 
.allow for precise control of how data is filtered, transformed, and retrieved 
.perform functions like:
    .comparisons 
    .logical operations 
    .arithmetic calculations 
.essential for crafting effective and efficient queries 



Aggregate functions 
.condense large datasets into single, meaningful values 
.perform calculations like:
    .finding the average salary
    .counting the number of customers
    .identifying the highest product price 



Data constraints 
.keep data accurate by setting rules for can be stored 
.prevent invalid entries like:
    .missing values
    .duplicates 
.ensure reliable data 


Joining data 
.combine data from multiple tables 
.merge rows based on matching values, letting me see connections and gain insights I wouldn't get from separate tables 


Functions 
.powerful tools to manipulate and analyze data 
.perform various tasks:
    .mathematical calculations 
    .string manipulations
    .data and time operations
    .data aggregation 
.leverage them to efficiently transform and analyze data and extract valuable insights 


Views
.act like virtual tables, simplifying complex queries 
>more like pre-written queries I can reference easily 
.make my DB interactions more efficient 


Indexes 
